# Allowlist, not a blocklist: the image needs exactly the two files the
# Dockerfile COPYs. The build context is streamed to the remote daemon over SSH,
# so this keeps it small — and a new directory, a virtualenv or a secret file
# (.env.*, deploy.env, .mcp.json) can never end up in it by being forgotten here.
*
!server.py
!requirements.txt
